  "preamble": "Shift of the voiced retroflex fricative [ʐ] to the postalveolar fricative [ʒ]. It is documented in Kartvelian, where Proto-Kartvelian *z₁ (reconstructed as [ʐ] in the Gamkrelidze-Machavariani system) became ž [ʒ] in Mingrelian, Laz and Svan, while Georgian merged it with plain z.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Deretroflexion, Merger",
  "languageExamples": [
    {
      "language": "Proto-Kartvelian to Mingrelian and Laz",
      "languageFamily": "Zan",
      "examples": [
        {
          "from": "Proto-Kartvelian *mz₁e- 'sun' (Old Georgian მზჱ mzē)",
          "to": "Mingrelian ბჟა bža, Laz ბჟაჩხა bžačxa"
        },
        {
          "from": "Proto-Kartvelian *q̇wiz₁- 'liver'",
          "to": "Mingrelian ყვიჟი q̇viži",
          "note": "ž is the Kartvelological transcription of [ʒ]. Wiktionary's subscript-1 series (*s₁, *z₁, *c₁, *ʒ₁) is the Gamkrelidze-Machavariani 'hissing-hushing' series, given in the Wikipedia Proto-Kartvelian consonant table (after Gamkrelidze 1966 and Fähnrich 2002) as retroflex [ʂ ʐ ʈ͡ʂ ɖ͡ʐ]."
        }
      ]
    },
